# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-7, 2.1-21). L §3.6 The arrival rule: "The shares of one arrival sum to exactly 1, or the
# arrival is refused (RUN-LABEL, naming the movement)"; E §4.2 step 5: a refused leg isn't booked, and the place's
# balance is refused from that point. wage's shares are ania's half and no one else's: 0.5. Before it, konto is its
# opening.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
input half: num
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order if k.owner == ania_tomek then 0 else 1
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input wage_day: date
input wage_amt: money PLN
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule base = if p == ania then half else 0
move wage: transfers
  on wage_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount wage_amt
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-31), bal(konto, 2026-01-31), bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of ania

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  half = 0.5
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  wage_day = 2026-02-01
  wage_amt = 100.00 PLN
=== expect
q: (refused: RUN-LABEL the shares of wage's arrival at konto sum to 0.5, not 1, 0.00 PLN, refused: RUN-LABEL the shares of wage's arrival at konto sum to 0.5, not 1)
  cut 2026-01-01
